A node format with regex characters such as parentheses matches its own titles and yields its content in Roam and Obsidian through one shared builder and extractor, and ordinary formats behave as before.
test-3-graph has the four baseline pages; Draft Claim (`Claim (draft) - {content}`), PK Pipe Question, PK Backslash Note, PK Source First and PK Versioned Claim node types with a page and a look-alike each; a PK cites draft relation type from Evidence to Draft Claim; and Stored Relations on. The graph is signed in to the proof database and is in the eng-2329-demo group. The Obsidian cases live in the eng-2176-obsidian kit.

